1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,502
Here's the easiest way to get a lab onto GitHub.

2
00:00:03,602 --> 00:00:05,943
You drag one folder into your browser.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,738
Each lab lives in one folder on your laptop.

4
00:00:10,838 --> 00:00:14,395
For Lab 14, it holds your script and a data folder.

5
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:20,447
When a lab gives you a CSV file, your browser saves it in your Downloads folder.

6
00:00:20,547 --> 00:00:25,811
Drag it onto the data folder in VS Code's sidebar, and VS Code copies it in.

7
00:00:27,567 --> 00:00:30,590
Finished an exercise or two? Time to upload.

8
00:00:30,690 --> 00:00:34,396
In VS Code's terminal, type the two commands on the screen.

9
00:00:35,096 --> 00:00:38,013
The second one is different on a Mac and on Windows.

10
00:00:38,913 --> 00:00:43,195
A window opens on your home folder, and your lab folder is right there.

11
00:00:44,933 --> 00:00:47,061
Now open your repo on GitHub.

12
00:00:47,161 --> 00:00:49,544
Click Add file, then Upload files.

13
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,321
Put the two windows side by side.

14
00:00:53,821 --> 00:00:57,100
Drag your whole lab folder onto the box, and let go.

15
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,998
GitHub lists every file inside it.

16
00:01:01,733 --> 00:01:04,970
Scroll down. GitHub's default message is fine.

17
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:07,625
Click the green Commit changes button.

18
00:01:09,367 --> 00:01:12,731
Your repo now shows your lab folder next to the readme.

19
00:01:12,831 --> 00:01:16,345
Click it to check that your script and data folder are inside.

20
00:01:16,745 --> 00:01:19,257
That's exactly what your instructor expects.

21
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,941
After each exercise or two, drag the same folder in again.

22
00:01:25,041 --> 00:01:29,920
Files with the same name are replaced, and every upload is saved in your history.

23
00:01:31,367 --> 00:01:34,646
Before you submit, open your repo in a private window.

24
00:01:34,746 --> 00:01:39,924
If you see a 404 page, your repo is private. Switch it to Public in Settings.

25
00:01:40,624 --> 00:01:43,221
Then paste your repo's address into Canvas.

26
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:51,283
That's it. If anything goes wrong, the setup section in Lab 11 has hints for the usual problems.
